# One screen message of the terminal protocol fh.term.v1 (docs/terminal.md), as hex.
# crates/daemon (src/screen.rs) must encode its sample screen to these bytes, and
# crates/viewer (src/terminal.rs) must decode them to the same screen. Lines with # are
# comments. The bytes are written by hand from the protocol table.
# type 1, cols 6, rows 2, cursor col 2, cursor row 1, cursor shape 1 (block)
01 0006 0002 0002 0001 01
# modes: APP_CURSOR | BRACKETED_PASTE, fg d8d8d8, bg 181818, scrolled 0, history 3
00000005 00d8d8d8 00181818 00000000 00000003
# 2 rows. Row 0 has 2 spans: "$ " at column 0 and "ok" in bold red at column 2.
0002
0000 0002
0000 0002 00d8d8d8 00181818 00 0002 2420
0002 0002 00ac4242 00181818 01 0002 6f6b
# Row 1 has 1 span: the wide character U+754C over 2 columns (style 0x10, 3 bytes).
0001 0001
0000 0002 00d8d8d8 00181818 10 0003 e7958c
